WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.749 --> 00:00:03.550
- [Narrator] Are these golf balls?

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.880
A science fiction set?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.050
An alien invasion?

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.680
Nope, this is Bolwoningen,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.691
and the only inhabitants here are humans.

00:00:13.691 --> 00:00:16.274
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:20.830
Located in the Netherlands,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.010
about an hour away from Amsterdam,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.520
are 50 sphere houses made from cement

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.423
and reinforced with fiberglass.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.630
Bolwoningen, which actually translates

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.660
to bowl, or bulb homes,

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.114
was built in 1984 by the
Dutch artist and sculptor,

00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:37.023
Dries Kreijkamp.

00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:41.150
It was created and supported by a subsidy

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.373
from the Dutch government for
experimental housing projects.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.530
Inside the houses are three levels:

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.080
bedrooms on the ground,
bathroom on the middle,

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.743
and a living space on the top.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.260
Although these homes
look out of this world,

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.410
their intention was to bring

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.860
its inhabitants closer to nature.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.670
The round windows allow views
of the outside environment

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.210
from almost any angle.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.420
And the complex itself

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.280
is positioned near a scenic canal.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.960
The designer passed away in 2014;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.591
however, his legacy lives on,

00:01:12.591 --> 00:01:15.300
as these homes are still lived in today.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.883
(upbeat music)

